        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Four session types cover everything: <strong class="text-white">easy steady, intervals,
            incline and long</strong>. Most of your week should be easy, hard sessions should be
            rare and genuinely hard, and you should change one variable at a time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Starting out? Two easy sessions and one incline session a week is complete and
            sufficient. Turn up the
            <a href="/12-3-30-treadmill-workout/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">incline</a>
            rather than the speed unless you are training specifically to run faster, and trust
            your breathing over the console's calorie count.
          </p>
